WEBVTT

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:07.020
Captain's Log Stardate 7232.5. The Enterprise has spent the last two weeks mapping a previously unexplored sector.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.290
Long-range sensors indicate a rich uridium vein on the seventh planet of an uninhabited system.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.160
A landing party is investigating.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:23.380
Jim, I don't know why we're taking this risk. I mean, one false move and a chain reaction could blow away half this continent.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.640
Uridium may be unstable, Bones, but it's essential to starship construction.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.970
The source of this sector is going to be extremely important to the Federation for many years.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.960
Besides, I trust my people.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.620
He suffered a terrible loss.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.970
Premium meant everything to him.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.640
Duty leaves little time for personal pain.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.100
Or personal relationships.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:52.740
Like uncle, like nephew.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.380
You both ignore what you can't control.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.080
Grief? Family? Don't you see?

00:00:58.590 --> 00:00:59.970
No amount of throwing yourselves into your-

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.290
work is going to make either disappear. We were having a conversation. You were psychoanalyzing

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:11.380
robots. I wasn't listening. Preliminary scans indicate a rich deposit close to the surface.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.960
There will be a minimal danger in extracting it. Extraordinary find. Let's mark this vein

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:24.280
and wrap things up, Spock. Kirk 2 Enterprise, come in. Kirk 2 Enterprise, come in. Signal

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.580
is being jammed locally.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.510
What's going on at this?

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.770
Space, the final frontier.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.790
These are the voyages of the Starship Enterprise,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.040
its five-year mission to explore strange new worlds,

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.120
to seek out new life and new civilizations.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.300
to boldly go where no man has gone before.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.700
Captain's log supplemented.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.580
During a general mining survey on an uninhabited planet, we've been attacked.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.180
Security Chief Dickerson, dead.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.480
In orbit, a similar ambush.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.160
Reason are reasons unknown.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.370
Collector screens raised.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.260
Minimal damage.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.720
Weapons and shields are class 13.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.690
They're not acknowledging hails, Mr. DeSalle.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.090
Phase are set to one-half.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:35.920
Locked.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:38.520
Fire.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.810
Hostiles, weapons are offline.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:46.660
Ohura, try to raise the landing party.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:47.280
Aye, sir.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.230
Re-establish orbit, Mr. Kyle.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.830
Zahn, scan for human life signs and have the transporter room stand by.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.060
Still no contact with the planet, sir.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:00.690
Thank you.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:31.450
Damn!

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:39.500
Bones!

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:44.620
Alright.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.480
Hostiles have retreated, but communication links are still being jammed by a device on the surface.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.160
Find it.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:04:59.440
Who are you?

00:04:59.600 --> 00:04:59.960
Why did you-

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:29.820
attack us all your kind kirk here communicate

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.760
The location's restored.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:32.470
Kirk to Enterprise.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:33.690
Enterprise.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:34.460
DeSalle here.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.090
Captain, we've been attacked, but we're undamaged.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.420
It's an alien ship of unknown design.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.890
We disabled their weapons.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:43.320
We take a landing pod and are fleeing the system.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.130
Mr. DeSalle, the landing party needs an emergency beam out.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:49.750
Have medical and security teams standing by in the transporter room plot a pursuit course

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:50.510
on that alien vessel.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.820
Still no response to our hail, sir.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:05:59.970
We are falling back.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.480
Come back, Captain.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:01.460
Scotty.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:02.920
Don't read it faster, sir.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.110
We're stuck in the boilers.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:06.290
How's the captain, Bones?

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.330
Well, he's sedated.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.840
He's got a concussion, but otherwise he's fine.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.900
Now, your nephew, on the other hand, is down there beating himself-

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:14.660
The business of this ship.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:16.960
He was distracted on the planet.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:17.740
He could've been killed.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.620
Yeah, well, whose distraction are you worried about?

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.040
His or yours?

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:26.420
Now, you have an opportunity here to be a real father figure.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.970
Now, maybe you are more comfortable as his captain, but what that-

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.580
What I need is my ship's chief medical officer to tend to ship's business.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:37.200
We're at red alert. Now get the prisoner ready for questioning.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:39.030
Of course, Captain.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.210
Spock, hostiles position.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.880
They have exceeded our maximum speed and are slipping out of center range.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.080
Scotty, we can't lose them.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.380
But given it all we got, Sal.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.840
Captain, I'm reading several vessels incoming.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.080
Confirmed. Nine vessels similar configuration to the alien hostiles on an intercept course.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:06:59.380
Sal.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:00.690
Tactical report.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.110
They've got speed on their side, sir, but our weapons and shields completely outclassed them.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:05.160
They haven't got a prayer.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:07.680
Mr. Sulu, maintain course. Reduce speed.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:08.300
Aye, sir.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:11.250
Open a channel, Lieutenant. Let's give them one more chance.

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:12.110
Aye, sir.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:13.660
Channel open.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.840
This is Captain James T. Kirk of the Federation Starship Enterprise.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.760
We have aboard a member of your team from the unprovoked attack on our vessel.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.230
Stand by and pray.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.510
Unremarkable lasers and weak grivetic torpedoes.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:29.750
Minimal damage to our shields.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:38.460
This makes no sense. We'd have to lower our screens for them to do any damage.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.300
On the contrary, Mr. Chekov.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:45.200
They're concentrating their fire on one area near our starboard nacelle strut.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.570
They appear familiar with our configuration.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.830
They will eventually break through our shields at that point.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.820
Mr. Scott, reinforce the starboard shields.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.970
Chekov, half-facers. War them off.

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:56.840
Aye, sir.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.220
One alien vessel has taken heavy damage and is losing life support.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.780
Another has lost warp power.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.450
That's a warning, Mr. Chekov?

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.610
I'm sorry, sir. They're more fragile than I expected.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.320
Shields and starboard nacelle strut down 3%.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.540
It's like being attacked by a kitten.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.920
Indeed, but given enough time, their claws will do damage.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.890
I'm not just going to order their destruction.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:29.070
Why won't they communicate with us?

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:29.970
They must believe...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.780
that doing so would be less fruitful than their attack.

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:35.310
Security to sickbay.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.190
I want the prisoner brought to the bridge.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:52.120
Who are you?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.350
Why did you attack us?

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:57.550
My name is Alcar Kiril, adjutant commander of the 9th Peshan fleet.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:59.670
You will get no more from me.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.440
We're not here to harm you or your people if they would simply respond to our hails.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.900
Our hails have always been answered by insult and invasion.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.480
Why would we answer yours?

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:11.630
Impressive.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.690
Are you mercenaries or Alursa's new personal toy?

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:16.510
Alursa?

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.080
Listen, I don't know anybody named Alursa.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:20.480
We're not your enemy.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:22.210
You may as well kill me now.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:23.610
Your mescan mind tricks won't work.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.150
We're not mescan.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.440
We represent the United Federation of Planets.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.660
We're here on a peaceful mission.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.140
MESCAN MURDER-

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.070
Each interceptor!

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:39.560
V-V didn't fight.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:41.700
Captain!

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:42.490
There!

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.820
Murder yourself again, as the evidence against you destroys my fleet!

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.040
Jim, is that one of our ships?

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:23.010
Sir, the Eagle was lost eight years ago with all hands.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:24.070
On the other side of the quad,

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:26.370
there has been significant alteration,

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.460
armor plating, disruptor cannons.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:29.980
But it is the Eagle ca-

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.640
Captain, and she's attacking Pessian's ships with alacrity.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.890
Mr. Scott, extend our shields to cover them.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.280
We can't protect them all, sir.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:39.800
And the ones we can, it'll take some doing to maintain.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:40.400
Do it.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.860
Lieutenant O'Hara, try to raise the eagle.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.920
They're jamming all channels, sir.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.620
Captain, they're picking off the Pessian ships one by one.

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:48.860
Mr. Sulu, put us between them.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:49.530
Change course.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:50.670
213, mark six.

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:59.960
Another Pessian vessel has been destroyed, yet they can take

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.840
to attack us from within our own shields.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:02.700
Release him.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.900
Tell your people we're trying to protect them.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:06.510
They won't listen.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:08.750
They'll assume subterfuge.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:10.950
One Peschen vessel on collision course.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.130
Attempting the ram.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:12.850
Tractor beam.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.640
Damage to secondary hull.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:28.650
Shields are buckling, sir!

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:29.880
Damage control.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.560
teams decks 18 to 21.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.890
The passions are breaking away from our shields.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:35.590
Eagle is all the rancors to pursue.

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:38.640
They cannot withstand an assault outside our protection.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.420
Lock phasers on the Eagle, Mr. Chekov.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:42.820
Eagle now targeting us. Both phaser

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:44.520
and disruptor banks. Be basic.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:55.790
Return fire, Mr. Chekov. I want that ship to save you.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.200
It has a complete full effect against their armor plates in case-

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.210
Spock, the prefix codes.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:12.430
The prefix code may be intact, but normal ship-to-ship communication links are jammed.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:13.700
change our codes.

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:16.890
The Eagle, how long?

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:18.940
eight years now.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.110
You really don't know?

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.060
This isn't a trick.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.920
A trick? Commander Kirill, this is a nightmare.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.270
Who commands that shit?

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:28.770
Now.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:29.990
Alursa.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.280
vile, dangerous creature.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:34.660
She and her crew worm their way onto free vessels.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.540
twisting innocent minds to do their bidding.

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:37.960
Telepaths.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:40.750
No, they don't read minds. They're psychomorphs.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:43.160
Twisting the perceptions of others and...

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:44.940
forcing the will upon those who are receptive.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:50.340
The Mexican used to revile those with such power, but now they've risen for control and...

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:52.500
Castellers is the Savior.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.180
What do they need to be saved from?

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:57.210
We're not proud of it, but far in Pescian history.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.330
My people subjugated the mescon.

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:01.570
Lurs is now bent on revenge.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:04.060
Captain.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:08.240
They've devastated our fleet from 700 strong to fewer than 70.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:11.290
No matter our past crimes, this is not justice.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:14.640
Evasive means to evade, Mr. Chekov.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.830
They've reconfigured their thruster ports and impulse drives, sir.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.590
They outrun us at sub-light.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.190
Let's show them what these engines can do.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:22.140
Aye, sir.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:29.720
Boom!

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:34.750
Thank you.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:35.860
Dorsal shield's weakening.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:39.320
They've flown the long-range subspace transceiver.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:41.360
Centell, torpedoes. Deck 24.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:42.480
There's no armor there.

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:44.000
You

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.170
We've damaged their cargo bay, Section 3A.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:51.660
They're breaking off.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.060
Another bully on the block, Spock.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.080
They're not used to having a bloody nose.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.460
But there's no strategic value there.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:58.450
I guess there is.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:13:59.990
It's a cooling junction for their web.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.800
in subsystems.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.260
There's bypasses, but they may not know about them.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:04.300
Captain.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:05.560
The eagle is hailing.

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:09.100
It's a non-standard frequency. All other channels are still blocked, sir.

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:09.830
Stall them.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:11.360
Analyze that signal.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:14.590
If we can get into those computers while their weapons are down.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:15.210
Aye, sir.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:16.660
Come out a cure.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.320
We're going to set this right.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.380
I need to get back up there.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:37.150
Nurse.

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:39.580
Well, would that help?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:40.930
Yeah, me.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:42.780
paralyze your fingers.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.200
Where did you intern at Gulag?

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:46.890
I haven't killed you.

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:47.750
yet.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.140
And how are you doing, Mr. Kirk?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.120
Other than my destroyed career?

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:57.240
I wasn't thinking down there.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:14:59.960
I rushed out, got myself.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.420
of shot.

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:02.000
Stupid mistake

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:05.010
I endangered the whole landing party.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:05.780
The ship.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:10.020
I'm sure my uncle is drawing up the transfer orders himself.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:10.680
Yes.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:12.140
It probably is.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.790
We are in the middle of a space battle.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.480
two unknown attack forces.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.150
and the security guard.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:19.160
Who dashed?

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:22.830
instead of crawled on the planet's surface is foremost on the captain's mind.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:25.030
My actions could have gotten people killed.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:26.800
Perhaps it was a clever diversion.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:27.580
It wasn't.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:28.900
It was a mistake.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.040
Anson, if you continue to crucify yourself like this...

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.710
You're going to drive yourself insane.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:35.880
Listen to him.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:37.200
Speaking from experience.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:39.980
Certain mistakes are supposed to be a learning experience.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.440
If I don't examine them, I won't learn.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.780
And that's something that most people never understand.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:47.300
It's examine.

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:48.740
not dissect.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.320
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:54.660
Sir, am I fit for duty?

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:56.150
Yeah, but...

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:57.170
Your shift has ended.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.510
Take advantage of the down time. Doctor's orders.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.320
We're at Red Alert. I'm needed at my station.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.430
Ensign, someone else will cover your station.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:05.960
Give yourself a break.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:08.010
Go!

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:10.250
Save the galaxy tomorrow.

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:20.640
Mind you of anyone you know?

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:21.870
Yes.

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:24.670
But he doesn't need to punish himself forever.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:26.940
Of course not.

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:28.300
He's not Russian.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.490
Am I fit for duty now, Doctor?

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:35.260
Nope, but that's never stopped you before.

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.560
Go on, you're released, get out of here.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:52.900
We're in, sir.

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.670
They've replaced many of the computer systems.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.860
These changes are acting like a firewall.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:16:59.920
There's no remote access.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:15.700
from here sir then get me their logs as far back as you can aye sir done slacking i am not the one

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:22.380
who was malingering on extended leave there's more to life than starfleet my friend lies

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:29.790
captain we're locked out we've achieved some of the logs nothing recent

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.220
They're going to take some time to decrypt.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:33.800
Then let's buy some.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.000
Uhura, patch me through.

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:44.660
Lursa?

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:46.620
Fooled, Captain.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:50.100
She's quite deadly, especially in person.

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:53.590
I'll take that under advisement.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.930
It seems we've gotten off on the wrong foot, Captain Pike.

00:17:59.670 --> 00:17:59.970
It's Captain...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.470
Your library computers are out of date.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:06.680
Captain Kirk? You'll forgive me, of course.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:09.840
Of course. Now just return that ship.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:15.060
Oh dear. You're going to be difficult. How disappointing.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:19.940
Do you really expect me to give up such a comfortable ship?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:23.050
It's so cozy.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:28.170
Well, perhaps we can come to an understanding, Captain.

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:29.970
I could send a shuttlecraft...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:39.200
for you if you like and we could discuss an armistice of sorts here on my flagship i could

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:45.390
even give you a tour of the improvements we've made that's an interesting proposal but why don't

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:52.660
i just slit my throat for you right now and save you all the troubles you would do that for little

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:59.960
old me i've warned him about you alursa he's not going to

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.280
put himself in your clutches.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:07.580
Kara, I hope you're well, and how are the rest of your family?

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:12.930
Oh, oh dear, I miscounted.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.300
None are left.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:20.870
