00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:21.940
Beaming?

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:24.620
Yes, the transporters.

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:29.600
That is one technology that we have been unable to decipher.

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:34.050
Kirk, if you would be willing to let my technicians...

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:35.250
That's not going to happen, Captain.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.380
The codes are either corrupt or different.

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:56.260
Oh, he's a clever boy.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:59.970
I'm sure he changed them as soon as he realized we were...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:11.600
a threat. He's not like that blue buffoon. Kirk is formidable. Do you fancy him? Careful,

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:18.940
Andoc. A tongue as sharp as yours could slit its own throat. Remember, darling, one can

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:29.090
never have too many pets. Condrus, how long? Any moment, m'lady. She's no fool.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:31.730
She knew those codes would be changed.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.120
She stung me.

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:35.690
Why?

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:38.510
She may be waiting for assistance.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:42.500
Our intelligence reports indicate that she's developed a new battleship.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:45.450
Thought your vessel one of them.

00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:46.980
That's why we attacked you.

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:49.050
It's getting.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.780
They're effectively hampering our long-range sensors.

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:57.000
The disadvantage of their close familiarity with our systems.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:20:58.920
Evil is hailing again, Captain.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.250
I'm sorry we couldn't come to an understanding, Captain Cook.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:09.920
Perhaps we'll renegotiate when my boot is on your throat.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:35.620
Captain's Log Supplemental, the USS Eagle missing for 8 years has been found in the

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:36.980
hands of alien aggressors.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:41.610
Reverse engineering our technology, they've apparently created their own starships.

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.780
An enemy starfleet.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:47.020
Log analysis.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.940
An interesting amalgam of Federation and alien technologies, Captain.

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:54.350
They have less of the inveterate armor and weapons arrays of the Eagle.

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:57.120
Of course, she keeps the most powerful vessel under her control.

00:21:58.340 --> 00:21:59.980
Check off, concentrate your fire on the-

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:04.060
newer ship. Mr. Sulu, alternate warp and sublight attack vectors. Keep them guessing.

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:04.930
Aye, sir.

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:19.130
Take the Star Star. Not come this far against the Pesharn to have it all taken away by one

00:22:19.130 --> 00:22:25.430
Federation ship. Fight them, Endoc. Fight them as if your life depends on it.

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:41.130
Dex Seven, Section Two.

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:42.990
Damage control, Dex Seven, clear and contained.

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:47.320
Engineering on the ground, sir.

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:48.270
Scotty!

00:22:49.570 --> 00:22:51.390
We've got three-man power couple-ins down, Captain.

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:53.450
We rerouted, but it's dirty rigged.

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:54.690
They'll take an hour to repair.

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:55.650
Understood. Kirk out.

00:22:56.700 --> 00:22:59.140
The Meskin Hybrid Starship is disabled and drifting.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.320
Sensors detect seven incoming contacts.

00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:03.800
Pession design.

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:06.690
Carol, you've got to make them understand we're not their enemy.

00:23:07.620 --> 00:23:08.520
They won't believe me, Captain.

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:10.910
They'll send them under psychomorphic control.

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:14.150
The Eagle is changing course, turning on the Pession.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:18.200
My God, our technology's going to slaughter the Pession fleet.

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:21.080
Full scan of the Eagle's current configuration now complete.

00:23:21.660 --> 00:23:25.460
Reviewing it will take time, but it may provide us with an exploitable weakness.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:28.880
With Mr. Scott needing an hour, we've got to find a way to knock out our screens.

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:29.970
Those circuits...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.120
The rocket nodes are heavily protected from weapons fire.

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:33.570
What about a stimulus overlay?

00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:37.960
Possible. Such a flash will impair our sensors as well, however,

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:41.270
leaving us open to attack from both Pessian and Mexican forces.

00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:43.210
It's a chance we're going to have to take, Mr. Spock.

00:23:44.410 --> 00:23:46.470
I don't want to see another ship destroyed by a Starfleet vessel.

00:23:56.880 --> 00:23:57.380
What's happened?

00:23:58.200 --> 00:23:59.460
Sensors are down across the grid.

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:04.170
The Enterprise caused it. We cannot accurately maneuver or fire. We're blind.

00:24:05.320 --> 00:24:07.460
Then fire on Kirk's last known position.

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:09.960
Voril, get those sensors fixed. Now!

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:20.600
Sulu, continue on the preplanet course.

00:24:21.240 --> 00:24:21.980
Get us some distance.

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:22.770
Aye, sir.

00:24:23.870 --> 00:24:26.750
We're likely to recover sensors simultaneously with the Eagle,

00:24:26.930 --> 00:24:28.630
but the passion may rebound more quickly.

00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:32.440
Confirmed. They already have.

00:24:32.900 --> 00:24:35.960
Transfer all power to the deflector screens. Stand down from battle stations.

00:24:37.600 --> 00:24:37.920
Cell.

00:24:38.400 --> 00:24:39.920
They'll hold against the Pesshin lasers, sir.

00:24:40.720 --> 00:24:45.100
If we could get out of jamming range for 30 seconds, sir, I could get out of burst transmission to Starfleet Command.

00:24:45.780 --> 00:24:50.720
Captain, we can't wait for your fleet to arrive. Those new ships of hers will destroy my people.

00:24:52.650 --> 00:24:58.910
Lieutenant Uhura, get me the information from the Eagle's logs. I want to know how to hurt her.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:00.940
You have the time.

00:25:07.960 --> 00:25:08.300
Engineering.

00:25:09.980 --> 00:25:10.480
Decade.

00:25:12.670 --> 00:25:14.010
One of your officers needs his captain.

00:25:15.330 --> 00:25:17.410
I'd call that ship's business.

00:25:36.460 --> 00:25:39.460
Injury. Captain.

00:25:42.130 --> 00:25:42.670
At ease, Anson.

00:25:46.330 --> 00:25:49.580
I'd be on duty, sir, but the doctor has ordered otherwise.

00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:52.310
Well, doctor's orders can be a bit annoying.

00:25:54.710 --> 00:25:56.790
Dr. McCoy is under the impression that you need a little guidance.

00:25:58.320 --> 00:25:59.780
Maybe you're being a bit too hard on yourself.

00:26:00.030 --> 00:26:08.210
this incident on the planet. I'm trying to learn from my mistakes, sir. That was your order. Peter,

00:26:08.290 --> 00:26:13.260
that was advice, not an order. You might try listening to me a little bit. It might be easier

00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:27.250
for you if you just relax. Sit down. Lieutenant Chekhov thinks I'm overanalyzing. You are,

00:26:28.870 --> 00:26:29.970
and I know this because it's...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:36.040
another Ensign Kirk used to do. Listen, your distraction on the planet, perfectly normal.

00:26:37.050 --> 00:26:43.430
Your wounds, very raw. But there's no way he would want you to risk your life for his memory.

00:26:45.670 --> 00:26:50.260
No, sir, he wouldn't. Then don't. More than anybody else on this ship,

00:26:50.400 --> 00:26:56.210
I know that you came here to be with him for no other reason. That he's gone?

00:26:57.940 --> 00:26:59.880
You feel alone? Really?

00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:03.600
Peter, you're not alone.

00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:06.320
Nobody on this ship is alone.

00:27:09.540 --> 00:27:13.580
And you have a duty to honor his memory, living.

00:27:16.230 --> 00:27:18.470
Please don't let his loss be the weight that pulls you down.

00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:26.840
Is that what you would do if you lost someone you love so much?

00:27:42.920 --> 00:27:58.300
what I've done. I'd like to return to duty, sir, but the doctor. Yes, the doctor. What exactly did

00:27:58.300 --> 00:27:59.280
McCoy have to say to you?

00:28:02.390 --> 00:28:03.510
to take advantage of the downtime.

00:28:07.930 --> 00:28:08.210
Peter?

00:28:09.180 --> 00:28:10.420
That's exactly what you should do.

00:28:36.750 --> 00:28:41.080
waste my time, Laurel. If censors aren't restored, I expect for you to be working on them.

00:28:41.590 --> 00:28:44.860
I, Larissa, my apologies. My report, I've restored some...

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:56.770
circuits, but not all. With time. Time? How much time, whore? The time it takes to bandage a wound?

00:28:57.210 --> 00:28:59.830
I don't know, my lady. We've never done that.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.040
