00:29:04.250 --> 00:29:04.450
Stay.

00:29:04.730 --> 00:29:05.090
Don't.

00:29:05.180 --> 00:29:05.480
No.

00:29:05.690 --> 00:29:06.070
Me

00:29:06.300 --> 00:29:06.820
Yet.

00:29:07.090 --> 00:29:07.570
And you.

00:29:07.860 --> 00:29:08.100
too.

00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:11.000
you found.

00:29:11.350 --> 00:29:12.490
You know the consequences.

00:29:13.270 --> 00:29:13.970
Yes, my lady.

00:29:14.150 --> 00:29:14.970
That's your felony?

00:29:15.210 --> 00:29:16.450
No, I'll rescue the sensors.

00:29:16.750 --> 00:29:17.110
Immediately?

00:29:17.810 --> 00:29:18.570
You have my word.

00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:19.880
And my heart.

00:29:36.870 --> 00:29:40.210
Do you think the captain has someone in mind yet to replace Dickerson?

00:29:41.930 --> 00:29:43.050
I think we should concentrate more.

00:29:43.340 --> 00:29:44.460
on getting your sea legs under you.

00:29:45.160 --> 00:29:46.720
before vying for department chief.

00:29:48.490 --> 00:29:49.610
You have a knack for this stuff.

00:29:50.470 --> 00:29:52.790
Scotty will be eager to Shanghai you for extra work.

00:29:54.630 --> 00:29:56.130
We've decrypted the Eagle log data.

00:30:16.890 --> 00:30:18.610
813.2

00:30:20.630 --> 00:30:21.490
imperfection.

00:30:21.850 --> 00:30:23.630
You know, death in crystals.

00:30:25.240 --> 00:30:26.460
It caused an engine imbalance.

00:30:28.090 --> 00:30:29.770
He created a wormhole and sent us.

00:30:30.860 --> 00:30:31.600
Across the quadrant.

00:30:34.020 --> 00:30:35.900
Long-range communications are down.

00:30:38.280 --> 00:30:39.320
We have received...

00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:41.340
in answer to our distress call.

00:30:43.080 --> 00:30:43.680
a race nearby.

00:30:44.490 --> 00:30:45.530
Known as the Mesca.

00:30:56.230 --> 00:30:57.190
Plug Supplemental.

00:30:58.600 --> 00:30:59.120
You're a mess gun.

00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:01.560
The doctor warned me.

00:31:01.720 --> 00:31:05.630
It's an attempt to construct.

00:31:06.900 --> 00:31:07.780
Last resort.

00:31:09.210 --> 00:31:11.430
Get as many of them with us as we can.

00:31:41.450 --> 00:31:41.790
Dr.

00:31:43.240 --> 00:31:44.260
Captain, obviously, was.

00:31:45.030 --> 00:31:46.090
Alursa affected his mind.

00:31:47.180 --> 00:31:48.020
She made him do things.

00:31:48.970 --> 00:31:50.350
give orders he otherwise wouldn't have.

00:31:52.170 --> 00:31:53.030
crew was bound to follow.

00:31:53.990 --> 00:31:55.110
I've suffered the same fate.

00:31:57.450 --> 00:31:58.550
She was the captain in our fleet.

00:32:00.700 --> 00:32:07.400
Three years ago, Lursa captured her, twisted her mind, used her against us all.

00:32:09.960 --> 00:32:13.080
Lursa's order, Shadi killed my commander, destroyed his vessel.

00:32:14.660 --> 00:32:15.400
Further carnage.

00:32:16.540 --> 00:32:17.900
I had to give the order to...

00:32:21.800 --> 00:32:23.660
My wife's death was at my own hands.

00:32:27.360 --> 00:32:29.860
Lursa did more than deprive Shadi of her identity, Captain.

00:32:31.470 --> 00:32:32.990
You stole from me my life.

00:32:35.150 --> 00:32:39.480
When I thought you messed it, fate would be the same as Shadi's.

00:32:42.030 --> 00:32:42.850
I owe you an apology.

00:32:43.460 --> 00:32:49.420
No, we owe you for allowing our technology to be stolen and used against you in the first place.

00:32:51.470 --> 00:32:52.250
Options, Mr. Scott.

00:32:52.600 --> 00:32:53.240
Darn few.

00:32:54.070 --> 00:32:58.380
That blasted arm was a rhodidium derivative alloy, protecting our most sensitive areas.

00:32:58.910 --> 00:32:59.970
Scans of the armor's ca-

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:03.320
characteristics indicate a large fleet moving toward the Pesshin homeworld.

00:33:03.550 --> 00:33:05.540
Captain, you must stop them.

00:33:05.620 --> 00:33:07.080
We can't engage an entire fleet.

00:33:08.150 --> 00:33:09.110
We'd be killing thousands.

00:33:09.660 --> 00:33:14.430
We could have taken the Eagle back, killed the snake at its head.

00:33:14.830 --> 00:33:16.510
While its body devours my people?

00:33:16.960 --> 00:33:19.540
There may be a way to stop both Alursa and her fleet.

00:33:19.920 --> 00:33:24.540
A review of the Eagle's logs indicate this area of space is uncommonly susceptible to

00:33:24.540 --> 00:33:25.500
subspace disruption.

00:33:28.220 --> 00:33:29.980
Local subspace disequilib-

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:37.490
Where the Eagles engine output modified it would disrupt subspace in this area for some time rendering faster than light travel impossible

00:33:37.490 --> 00:33:44.020
They're not going to voluntarily modify their engines. It would take a save it or wait a minute

00:33:44.020 --> 00:33:51.420
This area includes where exactly we cannot know the location of every Mexican hybrid starship to be effective

00:33:51.420 --> 00:33:59.840
The disruption must encompass both star systems my god Jim that would isolate them totally. What if their colony?

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:06.680
can't survive without support. Millions could die on both sides. Mr. Spock, how

00:34:06.680 --> 00:34:11.820
long would this disruption last? Unknown. Many of our colonies would find

00:34:11.820 --> 00:34:17.610
life difficult for a time. This would keep my home world safe. And what of the

00:34:17.610 --> 00:34:23.540
Meskin? Who speaks for them? They can't all support this war. Those who don't die

00:34:23.540 --> 00:34:28.190
along with those who do? Such is the unfortunate price of warfare, doctor. We

00:34:28.190 --> 00:34:29.970
are not the aggressors. Yeah, well ask the

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:35.120
dead if they give a damn who the aggressors are fewer would die this way you don't know that you

00:34:35.370 --> 00:34:44.500
can't know that jim we can't do this i agree with the doctor we'd be making a decision that would

00:34:44.500 --> 00:34:51.220
affect not only this generation but countless generations to come we can't doom two cultures

00:34:51.220 --> 00:34:59.240
like this captain you argue for a posterity that won't exist should we die today commander this

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.540
This isn't the answer.

00:35:05.240 --> 00:35:05.640
Kirk here.

00:35:05.910 --> 00:35:07.230
Sensors have been restored, Captain.

00:35:07.830 --> 00:35:08.930
But the Eagle's already gone.

00:35:09.240 --> 00:35:09.680
Find them.

00:35:10.190 --> 00:35:10.670
All hands.

00:35:10.810 --> 00:35:11.450
Battle stations.

00:35:17.150 --> 00:35:19.610
Captain's log stardate 7232.8.

00:35:19.840 --> 00:35:21.780
Commander Kuro has contacted his government.

00:35:22.120 --> 00:35:24.560
They have approved the subspace destabilization plan.

00:35:25.060 --> 00:35:26.460
That makes my decision no easier.

00:35:27.040 --> 00:35:29.900
What's left of the Peshan forces have pulled back to defend their homeworld.

00:35:30.700 --> 00:35:35.140
domestic fleet that I must stop. If necessary, with the drastic measures

00:35:35.140 --> 00:35:39.560
spot as suggested. She's alone again. Target the Eagle. Aye, sir.

00:35:40.270 --> 00:35:45.300
Two vessels incoming. Hybrid Mexican starships. Time to intercept 3.2 minutes.

00:35:50.320 --> 00:35:54.060
Fleet 7500 souls.

00:36:00.600 --> 00:36:02.420
Nothing stands between her and my planet.

00:36:03.760 --> 00:36:04.740
We've got to get through that armor.

00:36:05.150 --> 00:36:08.630
Captain, it may be possible to strengthen our phasers enough to burn through.

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:11.500
We could reroute their power directly to the warp engines.

00:36:11.720 --> 00:36:13.560
Our relays aren't designed to withstand that.

00:36:13.980 --> 00:36:14.520
Bypass them.

00:36:14.940 --> 00:36:17.860
Aye, but the firing circuits will only hold for a minute or two.

00:36:18.100 --> 00:36:19.840
A minute or two will get our attention, Mr. Scott.

00:36:21.040 --> 00:36:21.380
Aye, sir.

00:36:25.300 --> 00:36:26.770
Mr. Spock, this plan.

00:36:27.710 --> 00:36:29.130
How certain are you that this thing's going to work?

00:36:29.690 --> 00:36:29.970
The problem...

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.720
The problem is not execution, but timing.

00:36:31.980 --> 00:36:36.300
In order for the Enterprise to escape the subsequent dead zone, the engine imbalance

00:36:36.300 --> 00:36:39.660
which created the wormhole and brought the Eagle to this system must be duplicated,

00:36:39.880 --> 00:36:42.500
and only moments before setting off the subspace disruption.

00:36:43.690 --> 00:36:45.510
Kirol, are you sure about this?

00:36:46.040 --> 00:36:46.860
Are your people sure?

00:36:47.480 --> 00:36:48.060
I'm not.

00:36:49.370 --> 00:36:51.130
I'm surprised they are willing to pay.

00:36:52.020 --> 00:36:55.710
There will at least be peace if neither side can visit war on the enemy.

00:36:57.220 --> 00:36:59.970
If we are to be trapped together forever, maybe-

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.040
Maybe it's just accounting for our respective crimes.

00:37:02.860 --> 00:37:04.040
I can send you home in a shuttle.

00:37:04.640 --> 00:37:05.520
You'll reach your colony in town.

00:37:05.520 --> 00:37:07.460
Captain, I was an astrophysicist.

00:37:07.840 --> 00:37:09.900
If my people were to be lost to space normal travel,

00:37:10.020 --> 00:37:11.640
someone needs to be outside the phenomenon,

00:37:11.720 --> 00:37:12.800
looking for a solution.

00:37:15.080 --> 00:37:16.360
I have no family to return to.

00:37:18.640 --> 00:37:20.420
What adjustments do I need to make to the Eagle's engines?

00:37:20.940 --> 00:37:23.890
Captain, I'm the logical choice to beam over to the Eagle

00:37:23.890 --> 00:37:25.130
and affect the modifications.

00:37:25.900 --> 00:37:27.660
Alursa's abilities may be a threat to you,

00:37:27.800 --> 00:37:29.540
while my Vulcan mental disciplines...

00:37:29.540 --> 00:37:29.960
I need it here.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:35.730
Here. That woman murdered a starship captain and killed his crew. I'm going, Spot.

00:37:36.300 --> 00:37:42.580
It will take two saboteurs. Someone must route power to the proper circuits while the other modifies the plasma flow.

00:37:43.540 --> 00:37:45.660
Peter. Yes, sir.

00:37:46.210 --> 00:37:53.580
I understand that you've been polishing your engineering skills. Good. Because you're coming with me.

00:38:02.170 --> 00:38:04.330
They're cruising at warp 8 heading deep into our system.

00:38:05.400 --> 00:38:06.640
Increased speed to me.

00:38:07.990 --> 00:38:11.150
The drain to the engines will limit disruptor batteries and their structural integrity.

00:38:11.370 --> 00:38:11.770
Hand up!

00:38:13.230 --> 00:38:14.470
Intercept the Enterprise.

00:38:16.300 --> 00:38:19.880
Everything that I have worked to achieve will not be destroyed.

00:38:20.900 --> 00:38:21.500
You know why?

00:38:22.760 --> 00:38:23.080
Do you?

00:38:25.190 --> 00:38:28.010
Because you will not let that happen.

00:38:39.820 --> 00:38:43.090
Mr. Scott, request permission to assist with the warp phasers.

00:38:44.060 --> 00:38:46.040
Warp phasers? Is that what we're calling them now?

00:38:46.470 --> 00:38:48.450
They will be powered by the warp engine, sir.

00:38:49.090 --> 00:38:52.310
Aye. You lads finish these bypasses.

00:38:52.740 --> 00:38:54.200
I gotta get back to ruining my engines.

00:39:00.410 --> 00:39:03.590
Balancing the engines puts the lives of everyone on board at risk.

00:39:04.780 --> 00:39:06.260
Nobody knows that better than Scotty.

00:39:07.160 --> 00:39:09.200
What if it doesn't work, and there is no wormhole?

00:39:09.660 --> 00:39:12.560
We're sending out a warp buoy ahead of the destabilization wave.

00:39:13.320 --> 00:39:14.900
Starfleet will be briefed in three weeks.

00:39:15.370 --> 00:39:16.270
And we'll be trapped here?

00:39:16.780 --> 00:39:17.640
Not to worry, Ensign.

00:39:18.580 --> 00:39:22.080
There's a class implanted only 13 years away at Impulse.

00:39:25.240 --> 00:39:27.720
Mr. Chekov is the Eagle we want, even the odds.

00:39:28.190 --> 00:39:28.510
Aye, sir.

00:39:34.250 --> 00:39:36.470
Eagle is returning fire. All weapons banks.

00:39:42.550 --> 00:39:46.140
Casualty reports. Multiple injuries, Captain.

00:39:48.360 --> 00:39:48.860
Bridge to Kyle.

00:39:52.290 --> 00:39:54.380
Captain, I should really run a diagnostic.

00:39:54.800 --> 00:39:56.540
We need those phasers now.

00:39:56.910 --> 00:39:58.130
These circuits weren't meant for this.

00:39:58.580 --> 00:39:59.280
They're gonna blow.

00:39:59.500 --> 00:39:59.780
Kyle!

00:40:00.020 --> 00:40:00.520
Throw the switch!

00:40:03.640 --> 00:40:04.000
Captain!

00:40:04.310 --> 00:40:05.090
Phasers online!

00:40:05.720 --> 00:40:06.020
FIRE!

00:40:26.040 --> 00:40:26.820
Weapons Offline!

00:40:27.190 --> 00:40:29.170
hide them from the curse and jam their sensors!

00:40:37.350 --> 00:40:37.650
shot.

00:40:38.440 --> 00:40:40.680
Phasers torpitos the whole weapon subsystem.

00:40:41.100 --> 00:40:41.420
Gone.

00:40:43.270 --> 00:40:44.790
Kyle, get those weapons back online.

00:40:45.260 --> 00:40:45.760
Aye, sir.

00:40:48.230 --> 00:40:48.570
Aura.

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:49.560
Get me the ego.

00:40:50.820 --> 00:40:51.320
on spring.

00:40:52.940 --> 00:40:53.400
Alursa!

00:40:54.920 --> 00:40:56.420
I think it's time we meet face to face.

00:40:57.220 --> 00:40:58.660
We're prepared to beam you aboard the Enterprise.

00:40:59.530 --> 00:40:59.870
Captain!

00:41:01.460 --> 00:41:05.120
I had no idea what a developed sense of humor your Starfleet might have.

00:41:05.980 --> 00:41:07.060
But we flexed our muscles.

00:41:07.770 --> 00:41:08.650
We've tested each other.

00:41:09.270 --> 00:41:09.890
We've looked in.

00:41:10.200 --> 00:41:11.700
We've found our strengths and weaknesses.

00:41:13.140 --> 00:41:13.600
Let's talk.

00:41:14.840 --> 00:41:16.640
I'm sure we can come to some sort of understanding.

00:41:18.230 --> 00:41:21.930
So now it's my turn to slit this pretty throat for you.

00:41:22.970 --> 00:41:23.230
No.

00:41:24.570 --> 00:41:25.150
I'll come to you.

00:41:26.260 --> 00:41:28.460
This way you'll get a first-hand look at the operation of our transport.

00:41:30.380 --> 00:41:31.120
Captain Kirk

00:41:32.010 --> 00:41:33.450
You become more interesting.

00:41:33.900 --> 00:41:34.240
Oops.

00:41:34.470 --> 00:41:34.990
That's it.

00:41:44.040 --> 00:41:47.320
Transporter control has been rewired so we beam both signals in at the same time.

00:41:47.780 --> 00:41:49.180
The second signal won't be detected.

00:41:49.740 --> 00:41:52.600
We've rigged it for maximum speed transport to limit time shields are down.

00:41:52.820 --> 00:41:54.920
You have the coordinates to be mentioned Kirk to the Jeffers tube.

00:41:55.620 --> 00:41:56.040
Aye, sir.

00:41:56.900 --> 00:41:59.460
Keep a lock on those subcutaneous transponders at all times.

00:42:00.090 --> 00:42:00.810
And you.

00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:04.460
Try not to dig this one out with a spoon.

00:42:07.900 --> 00:42:08.340
Energize.

00:42:10.100 --> 00:42:10.540
Energizing.

00:42:19.570 --> 00:42:20.390
Two Kirks.

00:42:21.950 --> 00:42:23.320
God must be pushing me.

00:42:25.860 --> 00:42:27.520
If we were smart, we'd kill him now.

00:42:45.450 --> 00:42:46.150
He's aboard, my lady.

00:42:46.330 --> 00:42:47.430
We'll take him to the briefing room.

00:42:47.850 --> 00:42:49.270
My quarters end up.

00:42:50.280 --> 00:42:51.040
I thought that...

00:42:51.040 --> 00:42:51.480
End up.

00:42:52.580 --> 00:42:53.420
to do about thinking.

00:42:55.340 --> 00:42:55.820
Just-

00:42:56.330 --> 00:42:57.170
as I say.

00:43:01.050 --> 00:43:02.030
Thank you.

00:43:17.020 --> 00:43:17.960
change Mr. Spock.

00:43:18.390 --> 00:43:20.390
We can't maintain a lock on the captain's transponder.

00:43:21.690 --> 00:43:23.130
We've done everything we can to boost the signal.

00:43:24.220 --> 00:43:26.000
The armor is interfering with the transmission.

00:43:26.620 --> 00:43:27.240
What about Peter?

00:43:39.720 --> 00:43:40.340
on Edson Kirk.

00:43:41.060 --> 00:43:42.420
He's in a less protected section.

00:43:43.820 --> 00:43:47.520
Mr. Spock, if we can reach the captain by communicator to establish his general position.

00:43:47.980 --> 00:43:49.860
and keep the shields down 75% longer.

00:43:50.180 --> 00:43:53.720
That would leave the Enterprise open to heavy attacks should the Eagle restore her weapons.

00:43:54.090 --> 00:43:56.010
Spock, we are not leaving Jim behind.

00:43:56.490 --> 00:43:57.650
We cannot locate him, Doc.

00:44:06.780 --> 00:44:19.080
Captain Kirk! Well, in person at last. Truly here to talk, or are you secretly planning to kill me?

00:44:19.900 --> 00:44:22.100
Well, telling you would take away half the challenge, wouldn't it?

00:44:22.300 --> 00:44:25.510
Oh, we are two of a kind.

00:44:26.500 --> 00:44:28.480
Why don't we just start with a tour of your modifications?

00:44:31.050 --> 00:44:32.450
I have something else in mind.

00:44:33.630 --> 00:44:34.230
A lursa?

00:44:34.490 --> 00:44:35.750
Do not question me, Ander,

00:44:36.230 --> 00:44:40.230
or your next visit to these quarters will be far less pleasant than usual.

00:44:48.320 --> 00:44:48.800
No guards?

00:44:50.030 --> 00:44:50.430
Flattered.

00:45:01.920 --> 00:45:06.540
You don't strike me as a type of man who would hurt a defenseless lady.

00:45:15.390 --> 00:45:20.420
You don't strike me as a lady who's defenseless.

00:45:21.860 --> 00:45:23.220
You are right about one thing.

00:45:24.840 --> 00:45:26.950
I'm anything but defenseless.

00:45:32.780 --> 00:45:35.630
You see we are the same, don't you?

00:45:36.930 --> 00:45:41.090
Yes, we are, but not exactly.

00:45:43.780 --> 00:45:45.480
I'm glad you noticed, Captain.

00:45:47.160 --> 00:45:47.700
Call me Jim.

00:45:54.490 --> 00:45:55.470
Call me Alursa.

00:45:57.490 --> 00:45:59.980
Jim, you're going to tell me...

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:01.100
why you're here.

00:46:02.550 --> 00:46:05.090
Well, I'd like to.

00:46:05.350 --> 00:46:05.670
Yes.

00:46:10.510 --> 00:46:10.930
Can't.

00:46:11.320 --> 00:46:11.800
You can.

00:46:12.670 --> 00:46:17.090
Jim, you trusted me the moment we met.

00:46:19.860 --> 00:46:20.300
Trusted you?

00:46:39.880 --> 00:46:41.360
Modifications complete, Mr. Spock.

00:46:42.790 --> 00:46:44.910
Acknowledged to activate Mr. Centell's signal

00:46:44.910 --> 00:46:46.190
for transporter coordination.

00:46:46.490 --> 00:46:48.530
Peter, the captain's transponder isn't working.

00:46:48.710 --> 00:46:50.540
Mr. Spock, stand by.

00:46:50.800 --> 00:46:52.220
I can set this to trigger remotely.

00:46:52.420 --> 00:46:57.140
I'm gonna find the captain.

00:47:06.720 --> 00:47:12.450
Jim, Jim, I think it's time for you to tell me why you're here.

00:47:13.140 --> 00:47:18.420
Your armor, modifications, it would take us years to learn about them, please.

00:47:20.080 --> 00:47:21.780
I came to get the information from Starfleet.

00:47:25.980 --> 00:47:29.980
Jim would have been very, very...

00:47:30.860 --> 00:47:35.990
very naughty. You should beg forgiveness, shouldn't you?

00:47:37.020 --> 00:47:40.020
I should. Yes. I should. Yes.

00:47:41.030 --> 00:47:46.520
Transporter. I want it. I can show you how to fix it.

00:47:50.520 --> 00:47:56.980
Show me. Show me to have more power and all will be forgiven.

00:48:02.240 --> 00:48:02.620
Yes.

00:48:02.870 --> 00:48:03.350
I'll show him.

00:48:03.700 --> 00:48:04.020
Yes.

00:48:08.340 --> 00:48:08.740
It's all right.

00:48:15.970 --> 00:48:16.840
You couldn't have.

00:48:17.480 --> 00:48:18.240
Oh, I wouldn't have.

00:48:19.160 --> 00:48:19.620
Would you?

00:48:28.050 --> 00:48:29.210
Somehow I knew I'd find you here.

00:48:30.890 --> 00:48:31.290
What happened?

00:48:31.860 --> 00:48:32.220
Exhaustion.

00:48:32.410 --> 00:48:33.050
What are you doing here?

00:48:33.260 --> 00:48:34.600
There's no signal from your transponder.

00:48:35.060 --> 00:48:38.190
I've set the disruption to trigger my remote inside.

00:48:48.360 --> 00:48:49.020
Hold signals now.

00:48:49.930 --> 00:48:51.890
They've restored weapons and are charging all ports.

00:48:55.120 --> 00:48:56.600
The imbalance will begin at warp one.

00:48:56.910 --> 00:48:58.450
But if they fire, they're disruptors.

00:48:58.670 --> 00:48:59.490
Take evasive action.

00:49:03.070 --> 00:49:06.910
Eagle's engines are whining like a toy. We've got less than 50 seconds.

00:49:12.120 --> 00:49:15.140
Transporter room, prepare to energize. Lower the shields.

00:49:15.810 --> 00:49:18.330
Mr. Centel, you have 42.9 seconds.

00:49:30.730 --> 00:49:31.950
We've got the Mr. Spock.

00:49:33.330 --> 00:49:33.910
Shields up.

00:49:34.760 --> 00:49:36.420
Launch the Warp Bully, Mr. Chekov.

00:49:36.620 --> 00:49:38.100
Mr. Sulu, Warp 1.

00:50:28.410 --> 00:50:29.970
Exactly 3 parsecs from starbase.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:33.300
I thought we might need the benefit of their repair facilities.

00:50:34.560 --> 00:50:35.280
Did you kill her?

00:50:37.460 --> 00:50:38.360
She's stranded, Commander.

00:50:39.860 --> 00:50:40.300
Powerless.

00:50:44.480 --> 00:50:45.300
I'd call that justice.

00:50:47.090 --> 00:50:48.450
A shallow justice, Captain.

00:50:52.040 --> 00:50:54.540
Captain's log stardate 7233.1.

00:50:55.050 --> 00:50:56.270
Repairs are almost complete.

00:50:56.980 --> 00:50:59.800
Starfleet has gathered a task force which will be heading for Pesh in space.

00:51:00.440 --> 00:51:04.560
Probes detect the dead zone, blanketing the entirety of the Pessian and Meskin systems.

00:51:04.940 --> 00:51:07.060
For how long? We can't be sure.

00:51:11.180 --> 00:51:11.380
Gun.

00:51:15.250 --> 00:51:16.610
You wanted to see me, sir.

00:51:19.720 --> 00:51:20.180
Yes, I did.

00:51:22.410 --> 00:51:25.030
To check off your idea to channel the phasers through the main warp engines.

00:51:26.640 --> 00:51:29.160
Do you realize it destroyed the entire weapons subsystems?

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:34.400
Yes, sir, I. I'm aware of that. I'm sorry, sir.

00:51:34.930 --> 00:51:38.700
You saved the ship. You saved my life on the planet.

00:51:39.540 --> 00:51:42.000
Captain, I was only doing what any good officer would do.

00:51:42.380 --> 00:51:46.680
Mr. Chekov, you consistently see dangers to this ship and to this crew long before the rest of us do.

00:51:48.020 --> 00:51:55.070
You're at the navigation station. You strategize and analyze, see things the rest of us never dream of.

00:51:56.600 --> 00:51:58.480
You have a fatalistic heart, Mr. Chekov.

00:51:59.470 --> 00:51:59.970
Sir, I...

00:52:00.540 --> 00:52:17.200
I am sorry I have disappointed you, I'm going to make you chief of security in addition to your duties as navigator

00:52:18.920 --> 00:52:23.060
Thank you, sir. You realize of course this will put Mr. Kirk under your direct command

00:52:23.060 --> 00:52:27.600
I understand you've already taken him under your wing

00:52:29.380 --> 00:52:29.960
Uh...

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:31.340
Not that I'm aware of, sir.

00:52:31.990 --> 00:52:34.360
Well, he's gonna need a mentor,

00:52:35.080 --> 00:52:36.960
and I can't think of anyone more suited to the task.

00:52:38.540 --> 00:52:39.200
You know how he is.

00:52:40.400 --> 00:52:41.320
He's a bit too rash.

00:52:42.740 --> 00:52:50.110
Stubborn, competitive, he's way too hard on himself.

00:52:54.520 --> 00:52:55.580
Consensus on this ship is

00:52:55.580 --> 00:52:57.000
that he reminds you of somebody else.

00:52:57.810 --> 00:52:58.950
Yes, you.

00:53:03.610 --> 00:53:16.550
Captain, gentlemen, I'm glad we got a chance to say goodbye before I transport to the Lexington.

00:53:17.370 --> 00:53:23.840
People are safe and I have all of you to thank for, especially you, for risking yourself to

00:53:23.840 --> 00:53:29.860
a Larsa's powerful will. Well, she'd never met a Kirk before. We have will to spare, sir. And we managed

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:35.760
use it together. Commander Kirill, good luck on finding a solution to the dead zone. I shall be

00:53:35.760 --> 00:53:43.530
interested in monitoring the progress of the task force. There may be no solution coming. No, but it

00:53:43.530 --> 00:53:48.690
was necessary to stop the slaughter. Perhaps now both sides will be more focused on the problems

00:53:48.690 --> 00:53:55.540
that the dead zone presents rather than a war that can no longer be fought. Well, I hope that

00:53:55.540 --> 00:53:58.820
you see your home again and that your people prosper no matter what their conditions.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:01.980
Lexington signals. They're ready, sir.

00:54:10.460 --> 00:54:11.280
Safe travels, Commander.

00:54:12.250 --> 00:54:12.890
And you, Captain.

00:54:14.400 --> 00:54:14.800
Energize.

00:54:26.380 --> 00:54:27.960
Now there goes one brave man.

00:54:28.600 --> 00:54:29.900
The Peshan are a brave people.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:32.880
to have embraced a solution with such complex challenges.

00:54:33.380 --> 00:54:34.920
The challenge begins now, Spock.

00:54:35.680 --> 00:54:36.880
We're facing life in a world

00:54:36.880 --> 00:54:38.980
every day presents a new set of challenges.

00:54:39.680 --> 00:54:42.520
It's going to take a lot of courage to work together for the common good.

00:54:48.040 --> 00:54:50.330
Courage, gentlemen. The order of the day.

00:55:05.660 --> 00:55:09.440
This is James Cawley. Stay tuned for exciting scenes from our next Star Trek.

00:55:12.240 --> 00:55:14.900
Next time on Star Trek Phase 2.

00:55:17.790 --> 00:55:20.200
Something like that looks to be a nebula.

00:55:20.940 --> 00:55:27.010
Captain, sir.

00:55:28.720 --> 00:55:29.760
I don't understand it.

00:55:31.280 --> 00:55:32.780
I have not broken my vow.

00:55:33.130 --> 00:55:33.870
What's wrong, Assel?

00:55:34.640 --> 00:55:35.620
I'm pregnant, Doctor.

00:55:36.610 --> 00:55:39.490
That child may pose a threat to the ship in ways that we can't even anticipate.

00:55:39.830 --> 00:55:45.280
No matter how much Assel loves that child, it was placed inside her by an unknown alien for an unknown reason.

00:55:45.940 --> 00:55:46.320
Mother.

00:55:50.630 --> 00:55:52.630
Something is being beamed aboard from the alien cylinder.

00:55:52.990 --> 00:55:56.410
Alien energy beam is focused on impulse engine plasma cooling unit 2.

00:55:56.630 --> 00:55:57.550
Lock phasers on target.

00:55:58.370 --> 00:55:59.310
Locked on target, sir.

00:56:01.480 --> 00:56:05.810
Medical team to engineering, Lieutenant Ross has taken a massive dose of theta radiation.

00:56:06.140 --> 00:56:08.440
Do you have any idea whether or not she's connected to that cylinder?

00:56:09.420 --> 00:56:10.970
Why didn't we hurt you?

00:56:11.370 --> 00:56:11.770
Spock!

00:56:12.600 --> 00:56:14.540
I was intoxicated.

00:56:27.860 --> 00:56:29.880
It is an extreme biotoxin, and we were exposed.

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:36.660
to a lethal dose. Unless Dr. McCoy can counteract it within 6.2 hours, it will kill us all.
